 "source": "Kenney City Kit Roads (kenney.nl/assets), CC0 1.0",
 "license": "CC0 1.0 Universal. Kenney's License.txt travels with the meshes.",
 "note": "The city's *tiling* library (ADR-100), and deliberately separate from assets/city.manifest.json, which is the scatter library the ecology composer reads and which is capped at 64 layers. Nothing here is scattered: `world::placeCity` reads the `tags` to learn which piece dresses which cell kind, so adding a road variant is a line in this file. Only pieces that tile edge to edge on a square cell belong here -- a curve or a bend does not, because the lattice knows straights and crossroads and nothing else. preferredScale is 0 on purpose: the placer scales each piece by its own footprint so that one cell is exactly `moduleSize` metres, which is what makes two tiles meet.",
